sequenceDiagram

  actor PT as Patient
  participant APP as Reaktor patient app
  participant BFF as Patient BFF
  participant ITM as itsme / eID
  participant IDB as Identity broker
  participant CORE as Core service
  participant AME as Access Management Engine
  participant EHRI as EHR integration layer<br/>(Newwave Care)
  participant HIX as Chipsoft HiX
  participant LUI as Luscii integration layer
  participant LUS as Luscii Clinical Engine
  autonumber

  Note over PT,LUS: Patient login and pathway view (first-time and returning)

  PT->>APP: Open app (mobile or web)
  APP->>BFF: GET /session
  BFF-->>APP: 401 no session → redirect to login

  APP->>ITM: OIDC authorization request<br/>scope=openid profile rrn
  Note right of ITM: Patient completes itsme<br/>strong-auth on their device
  ITM-->>APP: Authorization code

  APP->>BFF: POST /auth/callback<br/>(code)
  BFF->>IDB: Exchange code → ID token + access token<br/>(OIDC token endpoint)
  IDB->>ITM: Validate code, verify signature
  ITM-->>IDB: ID token (RRN, name, DOB)
  IDB-->>BFF: Validated identity claims

  BFF->>AME: Resolve roles for RRN
  AME->>CORE: Lookup patient by RRN<br/>(internal API)
  CORE-->>AME: Patient ID, active pathways list

  AME-->>BFF: Active role = patient<br/>+ entitlements (pathways, shielding policy)
  BFF-->>APP: Session token<br/>+ role claims

  APP->>BFF: GET /home (pathway view)
  BFF->>CORE: GET pathway state for patient<br/>(scoped to entitlements)
  CORE-->>BFF: Active pathways + pending tasks

  par
    BFF->>LUI: GET Actions for patient
    LUI->>LUS: Query patient observations
    LUS-->>LUI: Observation bundle
    LUI-->>BFF: Get Open Tasks
  and
    BFF->>EHRI: GET Appointments for patients
    EHRI->>HIX: GET Appointment?patient=ID
    HIX-->>EHRI: Appointment bundle
    EHRI-->>BFF: Upcoming appointments
  end

  BFF-->>APP: Aggregated pathway view
  APP-->>PT: Render home screen<br/>(pathway timeline, tasks,<br/>appointments, content cards)

  Note over PT,LUS: All actions in the session carry the session token<br/>every request is re-checked by the AME server-side.